{"released":"1966","country":"US","labels":[{"name":"King Records","catno":"826"},{"name":"King Records","catno":"KING 826"}],"formats":[{"name":"Vinyl","qty":"1","descriptions":["LP","Album","Reissue","Mono"]}],"companies":[{"name":"Apollo Theater-New York City","role":"Recorded At"},{"name":"King Records, Inc.","role":"Record Company"}],"identifiers":[{"type":"Matrix / Runout","value":"K-12-826-A","description":"Side A, label"},{"type":"Matrix / Runout","value":"K-12-826-B","description":"Side B, label"},{"type":"Matrix / Runout","value":"K-12-826-A-X3","description":"Side A, runout, etched, variant 1"},{"type":"Matrix / Runout","value":"K-12-826-B-X4","description":"Side B, runout, etched, variant 1"},{"type":"Matrix / Runout","value":"K-12-826-A-X4","description":"Side A, runout, etched, variant 2"},{"type":"Matrix / Runout","value":"K-12-826-B-X4","description":"Side B, runout, etched, variant 2"}],"credits":[{"name":"The Apollo Theater","role":"Presenter"}],"notes":"Recorded live at Apollo Theater, New York City, October 24, 1962\n\nOriginally released in 1963.\n\nThis edition can be identified by its black labels, the 'crown' King logo variation, the back cover artwork, the last track, and by the mono format as follows:\n\nThe front cover with \"Star of Stars\" in marquee artwork found on the original version but with the new mono 'crown' logo label design that King Records adopted in 1966.\n\nThe back cover shows an array of various King-released album covers (on some versions it shows the full tracklist along with some credits and liner-notes by Hal Neely).\n\nThe second track on side B consists of a nine-part medley: unlike th original mono release, (which ended with \"Think\") the final track on this release is \"Night Train\".\n\nThe tracklist shown on this page was derived from the other versions and from the Both Sides Now (BSN) website as only an abridged version printed on the back cover can be found on the physical release.","images":[{"uri":"https: